```
Given I am viewing active todos
When I mark the first visible todo as complete
Then that todo is removed from the active view
```

Background: "I have todos "Buy milk", "Buy eggs", "Buy bread"", "the first todo is completed"
So initially: todos = [Buy milk (completed), Buy eggs (active), Buy bread (active)]
When viewing active: only "Buy eggs" and "Buy bread" should be shown.
"I mark the first visible todo as complete" → marks "Buy eggs" as completed
Since we're viewing active, a completed todo should disappear from the view.

The step "I mark the first visible todo as complete" finds visible items. But in my app, the filtering works at the model level by only rendering filtered todos. So "Buy eggs" is the first visible item. Clicking its toggle marks it as complete. Since `render()` is called after the toggle, the view re-renders with only active todos. Now "Buy eggs" is completed, so it should be filtered out. Only "Buy bread" should be visible in the active view.

The assertion "that todo is removed from the active view" checks:
```js
Then('that todo is removed from the active view', function () {
  const items = this.document.querySelectorAll('.todo-list li');
  let allHidden = true;
  for (const item of items) {
