        assert.ok(item.classList.contains('completed'),
          'Visible todos in active view should be completed');
      }
    }
  }
});
```

Since my app renders only the active filter's todos, the DOM will only have "Buy bread" (the remaining active todo), not the completed "Buy eggs". So `items.length` would be 1.
- `allHidden` would be false (the item is visible)
- Then it checks that visible items have class "completed" - but "Buy bread" is NOT completed, it's active!

Wait, the assertion is wrong. In the active view, when we complete an item, it should be removed from the view. If the app only renders active todos, then the completed item won't be in the DOM at all.

The assertion is checking the wrong thing. When the app re-renders in active view, it only shows active (non-completed) todos. So "Buy eggs" (now completed) won't be rendered. Only "Buy bread" (still active) will be rendered. But the step checks that visible items have class "completed" which is backwards.

The correct behavior is: "that todo is removed from the active view" - meaning the item that was marked as complete should no longer appear in the active view. So the active view should show fewer items or the specific item should be gone.

Let me fix the assertion. The active view should not show completed items. So when we complete an item while viewing active, that item disappears from the view. The remaining items should be active (non-completed).

