Now I also need to fix the `disposeApp()` method. The current code sets `this.window = undefined; this.document = undefined;` at the start, but then it tries to call methods on `w` (the captured reference). Actually, looking at it more carefully:

```js
async disposeApp() {
    const w = this.window;
    if (!w) return;
    this.window = undefined;
    this.document = undefined;
    if (w.happyDOM && typeof w.happyDOM.close === 'function') { await w.happyDOM.close(); return; }
    if (w.happyDOM && typeof w.happyDOM.abort === 'function') { await w.happyDOM.abort(); return; }
    if (typeof w.close === 'function') w.close();
}
```

This captures `this.window` into `w` before zeroing `this.window` and `this.document`. So it should be fine.

But wait, I need to be careful. After `disposeApp()` is called from `loadApp()`, the old window might not be fully disposed when the new window is created. Let me make `loadApp` await the dispose:

Actually, since `loadApp` is not async, I shouldn't make it async without also changing the callers. Let me keep it simpler - just capture the data before disposal.

